1
00:03:24,138 --> 00:03:26,406
<i>Hey, guys! Danger D here.</i>

2
00:03:26,473 --> 00:03:29,077
The Internet cannot stop
talking about Fall Girl.

3
00:03:29,143 --> 00:03:31,179
<i>Popular</i>
<i>influencer Shiloh Hunter</i>

4
00:03:31,244 --> 00:03:32,847
<i>and her friend Becky decided</i>

5
00:03:32,914 --> 00:03:34,782
<i>to climb a tower</i>
<i>all by themselves,</i>

6
00:03:34,849 --> 00:03:36,349
<i>and it ended in tragedy.</i>

7
00:03:36,416 --> 00:03:37,819
2,000 feet in the air

8
00:03:37,885 --> 00:03:40,121
<i>on a tower</i>
<i>in the middle of nowhere.</i>

9
00:03:40,188 --> 00:03:41,254
<i>We made it!</i>

10
00:03:42,724 --> 00:03:44,592
Did you see the video
that's going viral right now?

11
00:03:44,659 --> 00:03:45,960
<i>Danger D!</i>

12
00:03:47,260 --> 00:03:48,663
That clip, the one of the fall?

13
00:03:50,397 --> 00:03:51,431
Oh, my God!

14
00:03:51,498 --> 00:03:52,700
<i>Hunter, are you okay?</i>

15
00:03:52,767 --> 00:03:54,936
<i>You're gonna have</i>
<i>to pull me up!</i>

16
00:03:55,002 --> 00:03:56,804
-This should not be online.
-My heart stopped.

17
00:03:56,871 --> 00:03:59,439
<i>No way down,</i>
<i>and no way to call for help.</i>

18
00:04:00,842 --> 00:04:02,043
<i>You would have thought</i>

19
00:04:02,110 --> 00:04:04,545
that Hunter's story
would have ended there.

20
00:04:04,612 --> 00:04:07,648
And seeing Shiloh's tragedy
turned into a trend.

21
00:04:07,715 --> 00:04:09,382
-It's all over the Internet.
-Fans are even

22
00:04:09,449 --> 00:04:13,054
calling themselves
her fall-owers.

23
00:04:13,121 --> 00:04:15,723
Shiloh's crusty Bronco
showed up on eBay.

24
00:04:15,790 --> 00:04:17,357
<i>It's Hunter's famous Bronco.</i>

25
00:04:17,424 --> 00:04:18,458
It's just, like, disrespectful

26
00:04:18,526 --> 00:04:19,627
what these people try and do.

27
00:04:19,694 --> 00:04:20,795
Can I help you?

28
00:04:20,862 --> 00:04:21,996
Can I take a photo with you?

29
00:04:22,063 --> 00:04:23,197
No,
I don't want any photos.

30
00:04:23,263 --> 00:04:25,633
Amidst all the crazy,
crazy stunts she's done,

31
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:26,801
I think there's some real beauty

32
00:04:26,868 --> 00:04:28,236
in what she had to say.

33
00:04:28,301 --> 00:04:31,471
<i>You have to do something</i>
<i>that makes you feel alive.</i>

34
00:04:31,539 --> 00:04:33,574
<i>That was amazing.</i>

35
00:04:33,641 --> 00:04:36,077
<i>But don't worry, you'll</i>
<i>still be famous if you fall.</i>

36
00:04:40,447 --> 00:04:42,917
My sister talked a lot
about you.

37
00:04:44,118 --> 00:04:45,553
Considered you family.

38
00:04:45,620 --> 00:04:47,287
I'm surprised we never met.

39
00:04:48,756 --> 00:04:52,894
The, uh, police recovered it
a few weeks back.

40
00:04:54,128 --> 00:04:55,763
I had a lot of offers, but...

41
00:04:55,830 --> 00:04:57,932
Thank you.

42
00:04:57,999 --> 00:05:01,102
I'm not gonna sell it to one
of those crazy hardcore fans.

43
00:05:01,169 --> 00:05:03,470
I can understand that.

44
00:05:04,839 --> 00:05:05,907
Jesus.

45
00:05:13,080 --> 00:05:14,582
That's familiar.

46
00:05:20,588 --> 00:05:22,890
Oh-ho-ho-ho!

47
00:05:22,957 --> 00:05:24,091
Shit.

48
00:05:24,859 --> 00:05:26,326
No.

49
00:05:29,297 --> 00:05:30,298
What is it?

50
00:05:31,999 --> 00:05:34,602
You didn't watch
any of your sister's posts?

51
00:05:38,039 --> 00:05:40,440
It's, like,
her ultimate bucket list.

52
00:05:40,508 --> 00:05:42,910
Every single crazy adventure

53
00:05:42,977 --> 00:05:47,281
and insane stunt
she planned is in here.

54
00:05:47,347 --> 00:05:50,350
And she was trying to make her
way through it all, but...

55
00:05:51,384 --> 00:05:53,120
barely made it halfway.

56
00:05:57,692 --> 00:05:59,160
Do you mind if I take
a couple of pictures

57
00:05:59,227 --> 00:06:00,427
of these pages?

58
00:06:00,493 --> 00:06:01,529
No.

59
00:06:21,315 --> 00:06:23,450
Shi, I changed my mind.

60
00:06:23,517 --> 00:06:26,020
Oh, come on,
don't be a little bitch.

61
00:06:28,990 --> 00:06:31,025
I am not letting you
wuss out now.

62
00:06:41,002 --> 00:06:42,970
You know what? You can have it.

63
00:06:43,037 --> 00:06:44,338
Just take it.

64
00:06:44,404 --> 00:06:46,107
Take all of it.
You'd be, uh...

65
00:06:46,173 --> 00:06:47,474
You'd be doing me a favor.

66
00:06:47,541 --> 00:06:48,943
-Are you sure?
-Mm-hmm.

67
00:06:49,010 --> 00:06:51,478
I mean this...
this is all Shiloh.

68
00:06:51,545 --> 00:06:54,315
Yeah. No, please take it. I...

69
00:06:54,382 --> 00:06:56,150
I have a few ton more
in the kitchen,

70
00:06:56,217 --> 00:06:57,551
and I can't...

71
00:06:57,618 --> 00:06:59,854
I don't... I don't want it.

72
00:06:59,921 --> 00:07:00,955
Hey, it's okay.

73
00:07:01,022 --> 00:07:02,556
Sorry.

74
00:07:02,623 --> 00:07:04,692
No. Don't apologize.

75
00:07:08,729 --> 00:07:13,634
The last time I saw that
was the last time I saw her,

76
00:07:13,701 --> 00:07:16,537
I... I said something
that I shouldn't have,

77
00:07:16,604 --> 00:07:18,306
and it's killing me.

78
00:07:20,107 --> 00:07:21,208
And...

79
00:07:22,410 --> 00:07:24,979
I can't think or...

80
00:07:26,080 --> 00:07:27,715
eat or...

81
00:07:27,782 --> 00:07:29,350
sleep or...

82
00:07:29,417 --> 00:07:30,450
Hey.

83
00:07:31,052 --> 00:07:32,286
Hey, it's okay.

84
00:07:37,124 --> 00:07:38,859
Consider it medicine.

85
00:07:56,944 --> 00:07:58,412
Maybe that's what you need.

86
00:07:59,613 --> 00:08:02,416
To finish something
that Shiloh started.

87
00:08:02,482 --> 00:08:03,884
What do you mean?

88
00:08:03,951 --> 00:08:06,354
Move on.
Get the closure you need.

89
00:08:06,420 --> 00:08:08,356
You can finish her list.

90
00:08:08,422 --> 00:08:11,292
Just one page at a time.

91
00:08:12,526 --> 00:08:14,595
We can even shoot it
on her camera,

92
00:08:14,662 --> 00:08:16,530
real Danger D style.

93
00:08:16,597 --> 00:08:19,033
Why do you even want to help me?

94
00:08:19,100 --> 00:08:20,434
You don't even know me.

95
00:08:23,971 --> 00:08:25,373
When I met your sister...

96
00:08:27,274 --> 00:08:29,276
I was...

97
00:08:29,877 --> 00:08:31,445
scared of...

98
00:08:32,646 --> 00:08:33,981
of my own shadow...

99
00:08:35,549 --> 00:08:38,285
but there was something
in her spirit

100
00:08:38,352 --> 00:08:41,288
that gave me the strength
to face some really dark shit.

101
00:08:42,790 --> 00:08:44,025
Hmm.

102
00:08:46,293 --> 00:08:49,663
Her next stop
was gonna be Thailand.

103
00:08:49,730 --> 00:08:51,465
The plank walk
of the Mount Kwan.

104
00:08:51,532 --> 00:08:52,733
The what?

105
00:08:53,968 --> 00:08:56,470
This was from one
of Shi's last posts.

106
00:08:56,537 --> 00:08:58,105
"The walk twists
around the Devil's Elbow,

107
00:08:58,172 --> 00:09:00,908
"which sits 4,000 feet
above sea level,

108
00:09:00,975 --> 00:09:02,910
"ending at a spiritual statue

109
00:09:02,977 --> 00:09:05,112
"the locals call
the Deth Dragon.

110
00:09:05,179 --> 00:09:07,516
"They say when you make it
to the dragon,

111
00:09:07,581 --> 00:09:09,216
"it eats your fears."

112
00:09:12,053 --> 00:09:13,320
Come with me.

113
00:09:17,191 --> 00:09:19,160
No. Sorry.

114
00:09:20,094 --> 00:09:21,195
It's okay.

115
00:09:26,333 --> 00:09:28,235
I'm not like my sister.

116
00:09:29,170 --> 00:09:30,571
I'm not brave.

117
00:09:31,605 --> 00:09:32,773
I, um...

118
00:09:34,008 --> 00:09:35,242
I have a job.

119
00:09:35,810 --> 00:09:37,178
And?

120
00:09:37,244 --> 00:09:38,579
A life.

121
00:09:43,951 --> 00:09:45,486
Do you?

122
00:09:45,554 --> 00:09:48,456
This is your moment to be free.

123
00:09:52,927 --> 00:09:53,961
Keep it.

124
00:09:55,162 --> 00:09:56,864
Think about it, Jax.

125
00:09:56,931 --> 00:09:59,667
It might be that point in time
where if you don't do it now,

126
00:09:59,733 --> 00:10:01,135
you might never.

127
00:10:26,060 --> 00:10:27,428
<i>Shi, look at me.</i>

128
00:10:36,637 --> 00:10:37,938
<i>Shi, I did it!</i>

129
00:10:42,910 --> 00:10:43,978
<i>Shi?</i>

130
00:11:57,451 --> 00:11:59,286
Wow.

131
00:12:12,333 --> 00:12:14,101
Hunter read in a forum
that we can find a guide

132
00:12:14,168 --> 00:12:18,272
to take us to the top
at a bar called High Spirits.

133
00:12:18,339 --> 00:12:20,441
What do you think
"Icarus on the rocks" means?

134
00:12:21,942 --> 00:12:24,445
No idea.

135
00:12:24,512 --> 00:12:27,181
Okay, so we'll have to divert
from the tourist walk

136
00:12:27,248 --> 00:12:29,618
and take the Deth Dragon route
to the Western Peak.

137
00:12:29,684 --> 00:12:32,386
Hunter's notes say
it's been closed for decades,

138
00:12:32,453 --> 00:12:34,388
too dangerous
for the general public.

139
00:12:34,455 --> 00:12:36,223
<i>Police have</i>
<i>stopped traffickers</i>

140
00:12:36,290 --> 00:12:38,325
<i>moving large shipments</i>
<i>of fentanyl, heroin</i>

141
00:12:38,392 --> 00:12:40,894
<i>and cocaine over the border</i>
<i>to Myanmar.</i>

142
00:12:40,961 --> 00:12:42,664
<i>The police checkpoints set up</i>

143
00:12:42,731 --> 00:12:45,165
<i>at Mount Kwan National Forest</i>
<i>have proved a huge success.</i>

144
00:12:45,232 --> 00:12:46,233
They have police checkpoints

145
00:12:46,300 --> 00:12:48,369
at the entrance
to the Mount Kwan trail.

146
00:12:49,738 --> 00:12:51,839
They take no prisoners,
that's for sure.

147
00:12:51,905 --> 00:12:53,040
They're looking for drug runners

148
00:12:53,107 --> 00:12:54,643
trying to smuggle drugs
over the border

149
00:12:54,709 --> 00:12:56,477
to Myanmar by the closed route.

150
00:12:56,977 --> 00:12:58,846
Oh, my God.

151
00:12:58,912 --> 00:13:01,750
We're just tourists
taking a diversion.

152
00:13:01,815 --> 00:13:02,816
Don't worry.

153
00:13:16,665 --> 00:13:17,732
Jax, look!

154
00:13:33,748 --> 00:13:35,916
Dude.

155
00:13:37,284 --> 00:13:39,086
This is so sick!

156
00:13:40,321 --> 00:13:42,122
Oh, man, that looks so good.

157
00:13:51,265 --> 00:13:52,266
Oh!

158
00:13:55,002 --> 00:13:56,504
A little rowdy.

159
00:14:15,189 --> 00:14:16,256
Sorry.

160
00:14:16,323 --> 00:14:17,625
Go around!

161
00:14:22,062 --> 00:14:23,565
-Hmph!
-Um...

162
00:14:36,043 --> 00:14:37,044
How can I help you?

163
00:14:38,379 --> 00:14:39,814
God. Um...

164
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:41,348
We were told that
this is the place to ask

165
00:14:41,415 --> 00:14:43,150
for a guide for the plank walk.

166
00:14:43,217 --> 00:14:45,520
Yeah, it would be,
if it wasn't July.

167
00:14:45,587 --> 00:14:48,188
Uh... Sorry.

168
00:14:48,255 --> 00:14:52,560
We were told to inquire
about the Deth Dragon Trail.

169
00:14:53,394 --> 00:14:56,463
Deth spelled D-E-T-H.

170
00:14:56,531 --> 00:14:58,600
Assuming that doesn't mean
the same thing in English.

171
00:14:58,666 --> 00:14:59,667
Yeah, it does.

172
00:14:59,734 --> 00:15:01,636
But that trail's closed.

173
00:15:01,703 --> 00:15:04,873
Dangerous earthquakes
made it very unsafe.

174
00:15:04,938 --> 00:15:08,676
The Eastern Tourist Peak,
that's open.

175
00:15:08,743 --> 00:15:11,880
But again,
you're in the wrong season.

176
00:15:11,945 --> 00:15:14,047
And it's
for experienced climbers only

177
00:15:14,114 --> 00:15:15,115
this time of year.

178
00:15:21,689 --> 00:15:22,923
How about a drink?

179
00:15:26,026 --> 00:15:29,029
How about "Icarus on the rocks"?

180
00:15:30,598 --> 00:15:31,599
Mmm.

181
00:15:32,767 --> 00:15:33,768
You sure?

182
00:15:37,070 --> 00:15:38,405
Yeah, we're sure.

183
00:15:40,542 --> 00:15:41,810
Shut off that camera.

184
00:15:51,418 --> 00:15:52,419
Talk to him.

185
00:15:55,155 --> 00:15:56,156
Okay, thanks.

186
00:16:07,067 --> 00:16:09,604
We're here
for the Icarus on the rocks.

187
00:16:22,182 --> 00:16:23,250
Take a seat.

188
00:16:27,287 --> 00:16:29,056
I'm Luce. This is Jax.

189
00:16:29,122 --> 00:16:30,157
Hey.

190
00:16:31,291 --> 00:16:32,292
Jon.

191
00:16:35,830 --> 00:16:37,665
Do you know what you're asking?

192
00:16:40,267 --> 00:16:42,770
We're looking for a guide, Jon.

193
00:16:44,639 --> 00:16:45,640
No.

194
00:16:46,541 --> 00:16:47,609
You're asking for someone

195
00:16:47,675 --> 00:16:49,577
to lead you on an illegal climb

196
00:16:49,644 --> 00:16:52,514
on the most dangerous trail
in Thailand.

197
00:16:54,849 --> 00:16:56,316
Is that a problem?

198
00:17:01,221 --> 00:17:02,222
Hmm.

199
00:17:10,965 --> 00:17:13,133
Only for your bank account.

200
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:17,939
I mean, we could
maybe stretch to 3,000

201
00:17:18,006 --> 00:17:19,908
but nowhere near this.

202
00:17:23,545 --> 00:17:24,546
Hmm.

203
00:17:28,348 --> 00:17:30,417
Look past those trees.

204
00:17:30,484 --> 00:17:32,020
You see that big
son of a bitch looking down

205
00:17:32,085 --> 00:17:34,656
on us like Godzilla's
pissed off big brother?

206
00:17:36,356 --> 00:17:37,692
That's Mount Kwan.

207
00:17:39,226 --> 00:17:41,428
And the trail
you're asking about,

208
00:17:41,495 --> 00:17:44,298
it's been closed to the public
for over three decades.

209
00:17:44,364 --> 00:17:46,300
If the cops catch you,
you're gonna find out

210
00:17:46,366 --> 00:17:48,503
you're not in Kansas anymore,
real quick.

211
00:17:48,570 --> 00:17:50,270
If you get lost,

212
00:17:50,337 --> 00:17:51,806
you're gonna find
the emergency services

213
00:17:51,873 --> 00:17:53,173
either don't speak
your language,

214
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:55,710
or...
don't give two shits.

215
00:17:56,878 --> 00:18:00,048
And this time of year,
wet season, if it rains,

216
00:18:00,113 --> 00:18:03,116
those planks are gonna be
as slippery as an ice rink.

217
00:18:03,183 --> 00:18:04,786
Anyone ever tell you
you have a way with words?

218
00:18:07,421 --> 00:18:11,793
Okay. This trail
is as dangerous as it gets.

219
00:18:11,859 --> 00:18:13,493
I can get you up to the dragon

220
00:18:13,561 --> 00:18:17,031
and back down the other side
in Myanmar before sunset.

221
00:18:17,097 --> 00:18:19,901
The number on the napkin
is a bargain

222
00:18:20,768 --> 00:18:21,769
and non-negotiable.

223
00:18:28,475 --> 00:18:30,210
Have a lovely evening, ladies.

224
00:18:33,413 --> 00:18:34,816
Wait, wait.

225
00:18:36,584 --> 00:18:37,585
We'll pay it.

226
00:18:37,652 --> 00:18:38,653
Luce.

227
00:18:40,253 --> 00:18:41,455
I can't afford that.

228
00:18:41,522 --> 00:18:42,890
It's on me.

229
00:18:42,957 --> 00:18:44,058
For Shiloh.

230
00:19:35,810 --> 00:19:37,879
Altitude set. Prepare to jump.

231
00:19:38,613 --> 00:19:39,614
Come on, Jax!

232
00:19:47,722 --> 00:19:50,390
Oh, my God, I can't do this.

233
00:19:50,457 --> 00:19:52,160
Yes, you can!
It's just a leap of faith.

234
00:19:52,225 --> 00:19:53,293
No, I can't!

235
00:19:53,360 --> 00:19:54,729
It's okay. Take a deep breath.

236
00:19:54,796 --> 00:19:56,764
Close your eyes.
And count to 10.

237
00:19:56,831 --> 00:19:57,832
No! 'Cause I know you,

238
00:19:57,899 --> 00:19:59,967
you'll jump at seven
or some shit!

239
00:20:00,034 --> 00:20:01,234
Oh! Come on.

240
00:20:01,301 --> 00:20:02,837
If you can't trust
your big sister,

241
00:20:02,904 --> 00:20:03,938
who can you trust?

242
00:20:04,005 --> 00:20:06,339
Okay? Ready?

243
00:20:07,307 --> 00:20:08,843
-Lean back. One.
-One.

244
00:20:08,910 --> 00:20:10,712
-Two.
-Two.

245
00:20:10,778 --> 00:20:11,813
-Three.
-Three.

246
00:20:54,555 --> 00:20:55,890
- Hey.
- Hey.

247
00:20:56,924 --> 00:20:58,358
You don't look very Hunter.

248
00:20:58,425 --> 00:21:00,094
Well, I'm not my sister.

249
00:21:01,028 --> 00:21:02,196
Right.

250
00:21:06,399 --> 00:21:07,467
Okay.

251
00:21:07,535 --> 00:21:08,803
Let's get you ladies kitted out.

252
00:21:08,870 --> 00:21:10,938
Harness for you, and for you.

253
00:21:14,742 --> 00:21:15,910
O2 tanks.

254
00:21:15,977 --> 00:21:17,745
These are not cheap,
so, do not lose them.

255
00:21:18,445 --> 00:21:19,714
Why do we need these?

256
00:21:19,781 --> 00:21:20,815
Mountain bends.

257
00:21:23,416 --> 00:21:24,819
Altitude sickness.

258
00:21:24,886 --> 00:21:26,687
Heights, they can mess
with people.

259
00:21:26,754 --> 00:21:28,689
Headaches, hallucinations,
nausea.

260
00:21:28,756 --> 00:21:30,258
Worse.

261
00:21:30,323 --> 00:21:31,826
You're not taking one?

262
00:21:31,893 --> 00:21:33,227
Developed a tolerance.

263
00:21:33,293 --> 00:21:34,294
I don't need one.

264
00:21:38,132 --> 00:21:39,667
Testing, testing.

265
